Package: DEXSeq
Title: Inference of differential exon usage in RNA-Seq
Version: 1.61.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Simon", "Anders", , "sanders@fs.tum.de", role = "aut"),
    person("Alejandro", "Reyes", , "alejandro.reyes.ds@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "ccp"),
           comment = "Maintainer until 2026."),
    person("Hugo", "Gruson", , "hugo.gruson@embl.de", role = "cre")
  )
Description: The package is focused on finding differential exon usage
    using RNA-seq exon counts between samples with different experimental
    designs. It provides functions that allows the user to make the
    necessary statistical tests based on a model that uses the negative
    binomial distribution to estimate the variance between biological
    replicates and generalized linear models for testing. The package also
    provides functions for the visualization and exploration of the
    results.
